      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T23:50:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find this hard to read, what about expressing their intention by extracting a self-documented method and splitting this into two calls?\n\nAlso, we should mention the issue here and why we are doing this.\nA comment is typically required when the intention of the code isn\u0027t clear.\n\nThe culprit here is making sure that the injector passed to the `sshModule` and `httpModule` constructors is *exactly* the same as in `sysInjector`, otherwise it could be the top-level injector (when ApiModule is used and creates a hierarchy) and that would result in implicit just-in-time bindings at the wrong level.\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n      if(env.hasSshModule()) {\n        addSingleClassBindModule(modules, sshModule);\n      }\n      if(env.hasHttpModule()) {\n        addSingleClassBindModule(modules, httpModule);\n      }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 234,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "23c42149e9497c6d70be2b0504f53cad10f3fc21",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
