      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T23:50:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be best to move all the assertion logic into the test method and not in the module. Typically the reader of a test is expecting the body to have the assertion, not jumping up and down in the file.\n\nBear in mind that the only code that isn\u0027t tested is the test itself: tests are to be read and understood by the reader, if they are hard to read, they are potentially wrong.\n\nAlso, having the assertion in the modules has led to the incorrect tests on the SshModule, but you did not realise the problem because the assertion wasn\u0027t in the body and therefore was never triggered.\n\n```suggestion\n   // Empty body: the assertions on the injected injector are in the tests body\n```",
