      "writtenOn": "2024-06-28T23:50:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This pattern looks unnatural: typically to have a body in the test that expresses the expectations.\n\nIn this case, the body is empty and you just give success if there are no exceptions. All the other tests do the same.\n\nBy reading the implementation of PluginInjectsInjectorModule at L50 you can then see the expectations.\n\nIt would be more readable if the module just exposes the values and you put the expectations in the body here.\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n    String testPluginName \u003d \"my-plugin-injecting-injector\";\n    autoClosePlugin \u003d installPlugin(testPluginName, PluginInjectsInjectorModule.class, null, null, null,\n            (plugin) -\u003e assertThatInjectedPluginName(plugin).isEqualTo(testPluginName));\n```",
